---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME, SITE_DOMAIN } from '../lib/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'summary', label: 'The short version' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'on-your-device', label: 'What stays on your device' },
  { id: 'third-parties', label: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies and storage' },
  { id: 'your-control', label: 'Your control' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data: no account, no upload of your resume, and everything saved in your own browser.`}
  eyebrow="Privacy policy"
  heading="Your resume is yours. We never see it."
  lead="This policy explains, in plain language, what happens to the information you type into our resume builder and cover letter editor."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p class="legal-note">
      You don’t need an account. What you type is saved in your own browser and is not sent to our
      servers. Google Analytics runs only if you accept it, and we never sell your data.
    </p>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_DOMAIN}) is a free resume builder, cover letter editor and PDF importer
      that runs in your browser. The resume and letter content you enter, the PDF you import and the
      files you export are all handled on your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-we-collect">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not ask for your name, email address or any other personal details to use the site, and
      we do not run user accounts. We do not receive the content of your resume or cover letter.
    </p>
    <p>
      Like most websites, the server that delivers our pages may keep ordinary technical logs, such
      as IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time. These logs exist to keep the site
      running and secure, and are not used to look at what you write.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used, such as which pages are
      visited, roughly where visitors are located and what device they use. See “Third-party
      services” below.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to include. We use it
      only to reply.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="on-your-device">
    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your drafts.</strong> Resume and cover letter content, your chosen template, colour,
        typeface and layout settings are saved in your browser’s local storage so they are there when
        you come back.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Imported PDFs.</strong> When you import a resume, the file is read by code running in
        your browser. It is not uploaded to a server.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Exports.</strong> PDF and Word files are generated on your device.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because this data lives only in your browser, we cannot recover it for you. Clearing your
      browser data, or using a private window, removes it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-parties">
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      To display the site’s typefaces, your browser requests font files from Google Fonts. That
      request is made by your browser directly, so Google may receive technical information such as
      your IP address. See Google’s own privacy policy for how it treats that information.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong>, a web analytics service provided by Google, to measure
      traffic and improve the site. It collects usage information such as pages viewed, approximate
      location, browser and device type, and uses cookies or similar identifiers to do so. Google
      Analytics does not receive the content of your resume or cover letter, which never leaves your
      browser. Analytics is off until you choose “Accept” in the cookie banner. You can change your
      mind at any time with “Cookie settings” in the footer, or block it in your browser settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not use advertising networks. If that changes, we will update this page first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
    <p>
      If you accept, Google Analytics sets cookies to tell visits apart and measure usage. If you
      decline, it does not load and sets none. We do not set advertising
      cookies. We also use your browser’s local storage for your drafts and for preferences such as
      light or dark theme. Those items stay on your device and are not used to identify you. You can
      block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and the site will keep working.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-control">
    <h2>Your control</h2>
    <p>
      Because your content is stored on your device, you are already in control of it. You can edit
      or delete it in the editor, or remove everything at once by clearing this site’s data in your
      browser settings. If you have emailed us and want that correspondence deleted, write to us and
      we will remove it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights over personal data, such as access
      or deletion. Contact us and we will help with any request that applies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The service is intended for people looking for work and is not directed at children under 13.
      We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how the site handles data, we will update this page and the date at the top.
      Material changes will be easy to spot, not buried.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or
      use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
